(D/'SCOPE.md').write_text('''# D4-3: closed M3 request classification before opaque-token handover\n\nThis library unit implements item25 on the existing typed R1 path in invocation.rs and its existing test module. No new path, inventory successor, dependency edge, public API, ledger/profile, RequestId draw, durable entry, I/O or production workflow is added. D4-T2 has no request carrier at M3 and row57 is unreachable. Each of the three accepted requests returns None. Closed destructures pin all admitted fields, five flags, mode and JSON format.\n\nIndependent preflight permitted I1: existing host RequestExcludedClass is the request-domain payload, rather than the manifest-class digest/arm type. I2 is also permitted: classify inside the only AdmittedRequest::admit constructor after step-list validation and typed construction, before returning the opaque token. This gives every future caller the required ordering, with existing Observation::ExcludedRequest for a future non-None result; Vec::new does not allocate. No production R1 caller exists yet, and no such wiring is claimed.\n\nPreflight r1 found that counting literal AdmittedRequest text missed Self construction expressions. The only subsequent production-source change is none: production remains byte-identical to r1. Corrected tests pin the complete reviewed production module SHA256 and explicit one-Self inventory/order, catching any future new constructor, alias or spelling change until item25 re-review and deliberate hash update. This conservative source pin is not a future Rust constructor parser; unrelated invocation edits also require re-review before changing it. The exact module has one fresh constructor, private fields, no production child module and a cfg(test)-only include. Derived Clone preserves a checked value. The added unclassified Self-constructor mutation compiles and fails the runtime guard. Preflight r2 independently cleared this correction.\n\nFinal lane-r2 uses its own fresh target, verifies fresh=false compiler artifacts at the candidate source paths, enumerates both new tests in the exact host image and runs both successfully before the full suites. Candidate host421 pass/4 ignored, baseline host419 pass/4 ignored, with zero failures; components194/194 both sides, no failures or ignored tests. Baseline evidence is the exact completed fresh run at product3c02526e, reused unchanged. All eight ordinary checks plus restored-focused pass: host/components warning-denied all-target Clippy, doctests, workspace all-target check, changed-file rustfmt, environment controls, operability source and lock, design verification. No current whole-repository or production workflow pass is inferred. The four baseline host ignored controls remain ignored.\n\nFive mutations are fresh: wildcard replacement, skipped classification and extra unclassified Self constructor compile and fail runtime guards; appended wildcard and added flag are specifically expected compile refusals under the accepted lint/closed-destructure pins, not runtime successes. Exact final source is restored and focused invocation controls pass. No false claim of five runtime mutations is made.\n\nAn initial lane mistakenly shared a Cargo target across worktrees whose source mtimes predated the baseline build. Its candidate compiler artifact was fresh=true and omitted both new tests. That candidate result is invalid and excluded. Only its already-completed baseline runs are reused. The single owned stale host test process, with no children, was terminated; its cancelled log/marker remain history. Final candidate-r2 is independently rebuilt, positively enumerated and fully run.\n\nAll D4-4 prerequisites, J3d/J2c workflow/projection composition, D3b-2 production gate, D5-0b/combined D5-0 and D5-1 dependency, CF/Linux and qualification remain open. The inherited operability owner-label expectation is still outside this unit; no full-repository-suite claim. No private413/keys/real installations/heldout/T2 access or private census run. The source-closure19 files and manifests/lock remain unchanged.\n''')
